sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: ADR 0244 task, DECISIONS R1-R4 (process.stop shape), official @swamp/cfgmgmt behaviors, single-swamp-node. docs/reference/metrics.md.
  %% status: reviewed
  %% command: metrics:exporter:enable
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  %% lane M icon=server pill=target tone=purple
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant N as Node 12<br/>gets the exporters
  participant M as Metrics Node<br/>Prometheus
  CLI->>GW: metrics:exporter:enable 12<br/>Node id
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `orbit metrics:exporter:enable 12`
  %%> - syntax: `<node>`
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - makes Prometheus on the Metrics Node collect CPU, memory, disk and container metrics from Node 12
  %%> - shows up in Grafana at `https://metrics.orbit`
  Note over GW: Check eligible, record<br/>preference · task #5140
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - your Node has an access grant to Node 12
  %%> - a Node has the `metrics` role
  %%> - Node 12 is an active, managed Linux Node with a WireGuard address; never a task VM
  %%> - no other exporter change runs for this Metrics Node; the Gateway holds one lock
  %%> Builds:
  %%> - the complete new Prometheus configuration, with Node 12 added as a target
  %%> Result:
  %%> - Node 12's exporter preference recorded as `enabled`
  %%> - task #5140 recorded with the full intent
  %%> - nothing has happened on any Node yet
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-metrics-exporter
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - starts one Swamp run on serve (Node 209)
  %%> Inputs:
  %%> - Node 12's and the Metrics Node's addresses and SSH host keys
  %%> - the exporter unit settings and the complete Prometheus configuration
  GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>task #5140
  %%> What you get:
  %%> - the task number, at once
  %%> Next:
  %%> - the CLI follows the task with `operation:show`
  SW->>N: Install the exporters<br/>node-exporter · cAdvisor
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - installs `prometheus-node-exporter` (machine metrics) and cAdvisor (container metrics)
  %%> - writes a drop-in so both listen only on Node 12's WireGuard address, ports 9100 and 9102
  %%> - starts both, and restarts them if they stop
  %%> How:
  %%> - official `@swamp/cfgmgmt` behaviors (apt, fetch, file, systemd) over SSH from 209
  SW->>N: Allow the Metrics Node<br/>ufw · ports 9100, 9102
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - adds firewall allows on Node 12 for the Metrics Node's address only
  SW->>N: Check the endpoints<br/>both answer on WireGuard
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - checks once that both exporters answer on their ports
  SW->>M: Publish the config<br/>validate, reload Prometheus
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - validates the new Prometheus configuration with `promtool` before using it
  %%> - publishes it and tells Prometheus to reload it while running (SIGHUP or its reload endpoint)
  %%> - no restart, so collection from every other Node continues without a gap; Grafana keeps running
  %%> When a restart is needed:
  %%> - only when the Prometheus container itself changes, which is a role update, not an exporter change
  %%> - checks once that Prometheus loaded the new configuration
  alt all steps pass
    M-->>SW: Prometheus ready
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - Prometheus is running with Node 12 as a target
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal event
    %%> How the Gateway learns it:
    %%> - its shared run reader sees the terminal event; Swamp never calls the Gateway
    Note over GW: Record result<br/>exporter active · task succeeded
    %%> Result:
    %%> - Node 12's exporter recorded as active
    %%> - task #5140 succeeds
  else a step fails
    N--xSW: unit or check fails
    %%> When:
    %%> - an install, unit, firewall step or endpoint check fails, or the configuration doesn't validate
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>error_code, failed step
    %%> The Gateway reads:
    %%> - which step failed and its error code
    Note over GW: Keep the preference<br/>failed · resume the failed step
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the preference stays `enabled`; the exporter is marked failed
    %%> - task #5140 fails
    %%> Retry:
    %%> - Swamp resumes from the failed step; finished steps don't run again
  end
  loop every 2 s until terminal
    CLI->>GW: operation:show #5140
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - asks for the task's status every 2 seconds until it has ended
    GW-->>CLI: status + result
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - the current status, and the result once the task has ended
  end
